#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
=============================================================================
  SPY PUT SPREAD STRATEGY — FIXED PARAMETER BACKTEST & ANALYTICS
=============================================================================
  Parameters (fixed, no optimization):
    Entry day     : 8th trading day of each month
    Min VIX       : 14  (skip month if VIX < 14)
    Short put OTM : 11% below spot  → K_short = spot × 0.89
    Long  put OTM : 18% below spot  → K_long  = spot × 0.82
    Stop loss     : 90% of max loss (close MTM if loss ≥ 0.90 × width)
    Expiry        : exactly 1 calendar month after entry

  Capital structure:
    Cash                    : $1,500   (100% margin eligible)
    SPY shares (fixed count): $15,000 worth at inception (25% margin eligible)
    Buying power            = cash × 1.00 + spy_market_value × 0.25
    Contracts               = floor(buying_power / (max_loss_per_share × 100))

  P&L accounting:
    • Premium collected credited to cash at trade open
    • At expiry (or stop): settlement debited/credited from cash
    • SPY share count never changes — only market value floats with price
    • After each exit, new buying power = updated cash + spy mark × 0.25

  Option pricing:
    Black-Scholes puts with parameterised vol-skew:
      σ(K) = σ_ATM × (1 + 0.45·ln(S/K) + 0.15·ln(S/K)²)
    ATM vol proxy = VIX / 100
    Risk-free rate = piecewise-constant Fed Funds approximation
=============================================================================
"""

